1
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:09,270
I've received a lot of questions about how to cut a long metal using the pass-through.

2
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:13,790
In this video, I'll use a 1mm stainless steel as an example.

3
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:17,670
Before cutting, insert the material through the device's side slots.

4
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:20,110
You can start from either side slot.

5
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:40,800
In this video, the metal is slid from left to right.

6
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:45,140
Before securing the material, ensure the distance is equal on both sides, right where

7
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:46,520
the arrows are pointing.

8
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:49,780
Otherwise, the material may have an angle shift.

9
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:58,980
After alignment, tighten the knobs on both sides.

10
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:01,940
Next, install a proper nozzle for cutting.

11
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:07,700
Here, I installed an ordinary cutting nozzle and use X-Tool air compressor with 600 kilopascals

12
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:12,820
gas pressure.

13
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:18,380
Open X-Tool software, connect your device, and import your design file, process the letters.

14
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:20,340
For example, the letter O.

15
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:24,860
If we cut O directly, only a circular shape remains on the material.

16
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:28,860
To preserve the ellipse inside, we need to perform extra operations.

17
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,220
First, add a rectangle.

18
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:36,450
Then, unlock the aspect ratio.

19
00:01:36,450 --> 00:01:38,530
Set the width to 5mm.

20
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:41,450
The rectangle appearance is adjusted accordingly.

21
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:47,350
Center the rectangle vertically within the letter O.

22
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:49,950
Press shift and click the letter O.

23
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:52,390
Click combine and subtract.

24
00:01:52,390 --> 00:01:55,950
In this way, the ellipse inside O is preserved.

25
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:59,830
Since the patterns are separated, we need to unite them as a whole.

26
00:01:59,830 --> 00:02:02,870
Note that the letters and the two holes should be hollow.

27
00:02:02,870 --> 00:02:04,790
Select the two holes.

28
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:07,310
Press shift and click the frame.

29
00:02:07,310 --> 00:02:10,750
Then click combine and click subtract at overlap.

30
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:13,270
The holes and the frame are now united.

31
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:17,030
Before uniting the frame and the letters, ensure that the letter layer is above the

32
00:02:17,030 --> 00:02:18,210
frame layer.

33
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:19,750
Click the layer icon.

34
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:26,230
The letter layer is now under the frame layer, we need to move it up.

35
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:29,530
Click the letters, press shift and click the frame.

36
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:32,710
Then click combine and click subtract at overlap.

37
00:02:33,110 --> 00:02:36,430
Here, we get the final design for processing.

38
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:40,350
As the pattern is too long for the canvas, we need to split it manually.

39
00:02:40,350 --> 00:02:45,010
First, rotate the pattern 90 degrees.

40
00:02:45,010 --> 00:02:48,890
Add a rectangle.

41
00:02:48,890 --> 00:02:51,130
Unlock the aspect ratio.

42
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:53,250
Adjust the rectangle position.

43
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:57,450
Try to split from the blank space to minimize subsequent calibration errors.

44
00:02:57,450 --> 00:03:02,110
However, in this video, if we split from this position, the pattern on the right side

45
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:07,390
would be over 600 millimeters long, so we can only split from the middle of the letter

46
00:03:07,390 --> 00:03:08,390
C.

47
00:03:08,390 --> 00:03:10,970
Now, let me show you how to split the pattern.

48
00:03:10,970 --> 00:03:12,410
Select the whole pattern.

49
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:16,650
Use control plus C and control plus V to copy and paste.

50
00:03:16,650 --> 00:03:18,630
Place the copied pattern below.

51
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:23,170
Then click the rectangle, press shift and click the pattern.

52
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:25,670
Then click combine and click subtract at overlap.

53
00:03:25,670 --> 00:03:27,630
Here, we get the left half.

54
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:29,790
Next, we need to get the right half.

55
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:34,790
Select the rectangle, copy and paste it, align the rectangle edges.

56
00:03:34,790 --> 00:03:40,750
Delete the rectangle on the right, click the rectangle, press shift and click the pattern.

57
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:44,110
Click combine greater than subtract at overlap.

58
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:49,150
Now we've split the pattern into left and right halves, but you'll notice four unwanted

59
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:50,670
lines in the patterns.

60
00:03:50,670 --> 00:03:53,110
Next, I'll show you how to remove them.

61
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:55,110
First, align the patterns.

62
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:59,310
Then, double click the right pattern to trigger the editing mode.

63
00:03:59,310 --> 00:04:01,230
Select the scissors icon.

64
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:04,070
Place the scissors cursor on the unwanted line.

65
00:04:04,070 --> 00:04:10,070
When the line color changes, click the line to remove it.

66
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:11,210
Click done.

67
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:13,310
Do the same to the left pattern.

68
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:14,490
Double click it.

69
00:04:14,490 --> 00:04:17,330
Click the line when it changes color.

70
00:04:17,330 --> 00:04:19,130
Click done.

71
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,130
And that's it.

72
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:21,650
The two patterns are ready.

73
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:26,980
We can use different colors to distinguish the patterns.

74
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:30,280
Select all and set parameters on the right panel.

75
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:33,480
Select cutting with fixture as the processing mode.

76
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:38,140
Select one millimeter 304 stainless steel as the processing material.

77
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:39,700
Click apply.

78
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:43,860
Select X tool, air compressor as the shielding gas.

79
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:47,240
Select two millimeter cutting nozzle as the working nozzle.

80
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,840
Adjust the patterns.

81
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:53,560
Click the red pattern and disable output, otherwise, an error will occur.

82
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:55,360
Adjust the black pattern position.

83
00:04:55,360 --> 00:05:00,560
Remember to reserve 1.5 centimeters between the edges of the pattern and the material.

84
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:06,880
Next, click calibrate the capacitive sensor.

85
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:14,300
Then click the material.

86
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:18,460
After the calibration is done, click the framing icon.

87
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:28,500
Press the button on the device.

88
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,620
Click process.

89
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:34,660
Read the instructions on the right panel and ensure that the cutting tip knob is set

90
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:39,940
at the value minus one.

91
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:57,010
Click start.

92
00:05:57,010 --> 00:06:01,730
After processing, wear heat-resistant gloves for subsequent operations.

93
00:06:01,730 --> 00:06:04,730
Loosen the fixture knobs on both sides.

94
00:06:04,730 --> 00:06:11,250
Move the material parallel to the right.

95
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:16,130
Next, make sure the distance to the machine frame is the same as before on both ends,

96
00:06:16,130 --> 00:06:17,810
as indicated by the arrows.

97
00:06:17,810 --> 00:06:20,210
Otherwise, the angle may shift.

98
00:06:20,210 --> 00:06:24,220
Remember to tighten the knobs.

99
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:28,300
We can see the half-letter C, along with two cut lines.

100
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:33,120
Next, move the red spot of the welding head to the joint point.

101
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:39,600
If the red spot size is large, ensure that its center aligns with the joint point center.

102
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:43,540
In the software, lower the welding head along the Z axis.

103
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:49,190
Click the downward arrow.

104
00:06:49,190 --> 00:06:50,990
The red spot gets smaller.

105
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:53,470
Proceed with fine-tuning.

106
00:06:53,470 --> 00:06:54,950
Back to the patterns.

107
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:59,590
Remove the black pattern from the canvas and disable output.

108
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:03,910
Then click the red pattern and enable output.

109
00:07:03,910 --> 00:07:05,990
Place the red pattern on the canvas.

110
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:09,190
Next, align the patterns.

111
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:11,130
Add an arrow pattern.

112
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:14,630
We can use a different color for the arrow to distinguish patterns.

113
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:18,880
Enlarge the green arrow.

114
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:21,840
Align the arrow tip with the laser crosshairs.

115
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:24,840
Make sure they overlap exactly.

116
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:29,400
To ensure accuracy, record the X and Y axis coordinate values.

117
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:33,400
X1 is 565.3.

118
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:36,120
Y1 is 20.7.

119
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:39,280
Next, just repeat the same steps.

120
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:44,780
Move the welding head to the joint point of the second cut line.

121
00:07:44,780 --> 00:07:53,780
And lower the welding head along the Z axis.

122
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:58,900
Next, copy and paste the green arrow.

123
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:01,960
Align the arrow tip with the laser crosshairs.

124
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:04,040
Then record the coordinates values.

125
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:06,880
X2 is 566.5.

126
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:09,440
Y2 is 320.6.

127
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:13,400
Now let's see if the pattern matches the two-point coordinates.

128
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:17,650
Align the pattern corner to the arrow tip.

129
00:08:17,650 --> 00:08:19,250
Observe the other point alignment.

130
00:08:19,250 --> 00:08:24,190
If the alignment fails, the material angle was shifted in the previous step.

131
00:08:24,190 --> 00:08:29,010
In this case, calculate the slope using the two pairs of coordinate values.

132
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:33,960
The slope calculator link is in the comments section.

133
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:37,040
Enter the coordinate values in the slope calculator.

134
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:42,970
The angle value is used for the red pattern adjustment.

135
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:46,970
In this video, the angle value is 89.77.

136
00:08:46,970 --> 00:08:52,150
Subtracting 89.77 from 90 yields 0.23.

137
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:56,490
In other words, the slope is 0.23 degrees.

138
00:08:56,490 --> 00:08:58,810
Back to the XTool software.

139
00:08:58,810 --> 00:09:04,210
Since the pattern is tilted counterclockwise, the slope value should be minus 0.23 instead

140
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:06,010
of 0.23.

141
00:09:06,010 --> 00:09:08,490
Click the blank space.

142
00:09:08,490 --> 00:09:11,570
The angle is now refreshed.

143
00:09:11,570 --> 00:09:19,350
Align the pattern corner with the arrow tip.

144
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:22,590
Now both corners matches exactly with the arrow tips.

145
00:09:22,590 --> 00:09:25,030
The pattern alignment is now done.

146
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:29,540
Delete unnecessary patterns and letters.

147
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:32,200
Remember to enable output for the red pattern.

148
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:36,420
In this step, we don't need to cablibrate the capacitive sensor again, but we should

149
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:46,170
perform the framing to check the alignment.

150
00:09:46,170 --> 00:09:49,450
If the alignment is okay, click Framing Completed.

151
00:09:49,450 --> 00:09:51,850
Click Process.

152
00:09:51,850 --> 00:10:05,590
Click Start.

153
00:10:05,590 --> 00:10:11,360
Loosen the knobs on both sides.

154
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:21,980
Push out the material from the side slots.

155
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,300
Now the cutting is finished.

156
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:25,700
Let's see how the joint point result.

157
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:29,760
Even though the alignment was manually set, the precision is quite good as long as we

158
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,500
follow the operation steps.

159
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:34,140
You can't even tell it was manually adjusted.

160
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,300
If you need to cut a long material, follow this video to operate.
